{"count":1,"next":null,"previous":null,"results":[{"code":"EMSR794","name":"Flood in Madrid, Toledo and Guadalajara Provinces, Spain","reason":"Due to the rainfall in the Community of Madrid and the provinces of Madrid, Toledo, and Guadalajara since March 8, extraordinary volume situations have occurred in certain reservoirs in the Tajo River basin (mainly Alcorlo, San Juan, Picadas, and Cazalegas reservoirs). This has forced those responsible to carry out extraordinary and high-flow dewatering maneuvers, which have caused the flow rate of the Henares River in the province of Guadalajara, and the Alberche and Tajo rivers, both in the province of Toledo, to rise. The increased flow has affected population centres and agricultural farms adjacent to both rivers, with severe flooding of homes that have forced the authorities to evacuate them. Copernicus EMS Rapid Mapping is requested to provide initial rough estimation, flood extent, Monitoring and damages assessment emergency mapping.","category":"Flood","subCategory":"Coastal flood","sensitive":false,"reportLink":"https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/5f1a857f9874483797fa9bf7e2648b6f","activator":"Spain|Ministry of Interior - Centro Nacional de Emergencias (CENEM) de la Direccion General de Proteccion Civil y Emergencias","eventTime":"2025-03-08T12:00:00","activationTime":"2025-03-12T16:11:00","closed":true,"gdacsId":null,"continent":"Europe","countries":[{"name":"Spain"}],"aois":[{"name":"Talavera de la Reina","extent":"POLYGON ((-4.255162 40.3039, -4.226891 40.315261, -4.209406 40.315576, -4.193109 40.30141, -4.185264 40.284326, -4.183457 40.266893, -4.188674 40.253733, -4.205758 40.238556, -4.225243 40.226939, -4.248612 40.21958, -4.268871 40.206368, -4.286473 40.196132, -4.302377 40.182047, -4.338631 40.162614, -4.370077 40.146897, -4.394762 40.133195, -4.427894 40.108928, -4.442329 40.084768, -4.459221 40.071162, -4.475128 40.059855, -4.49392 40.051431, -4.521154 40.041363, -4.54102 40.039491, -4.574272 40.036015,